  "wording_refinements_applied": [
    "Neutral B01 now covers actual supplier, adviser, investment and employer use with the old guide preserved.",
    "Recognition does not by itself authorise attendance disclosure/attribution; context can still identify someone.",
    "Member follow-through is explicitly optional in the concept script and payload.",
    "Funding purpose accurately names already commissioned/completed work and distinguishes costs from multiple legitimate revenue sources."
  ],
  "manual_review": [
    "All three minimum payloads are concrete and conditional on actual evidence, permissions, delivery and capacity; this design is not commercial validation.",
    "Five contractual market segments remain visible, employer-side use is additional rather than a silent change to primary buyer.",
    "Full commissioned report and project IP rights are preserved; proposed future customer licences do not reserve a Riseklix veto.",
    "Free practitioner research is intact; no teaser downgrade, artificial individual-only restriction or equivalent-copy second sale.",
    "Partner recognition/briefing differs from optional separately scoped access; no default identities, private answers, guaranteed meetings or editorial control.",
    "The peer-cycle value is more than hospitality, but no advice desk, unlimited support, fixed cadence or staffed bench is promised.",
    "Research-only versus remote/written versus event-supported comparison remains open; no four-city launch, price, conversion or recurring revenue asserted.",
    "The final funding-purpose clarification does not prohibit licensing an existing edition or cost recovery/profit; it prevents presenting existing work as a new study and separates costs, revenues and bundled entitlements.",
    "Discovery sequence and counting policy remain coherent; all actual exposure/contribution arrays are empty."
  ],
